insert into public.knowledge_chunks (document_id, position, content) select '00000000-0000-4000-8000-d0c000000012', 0, '[recipe:00000000-0000-4000-8000-0ec100000001] Lemon & herb chicken thighs. Bone-in thighs with crackling skin and a bright lemon, garlic and thyme rub. A weeknight staple that needs almost no attention. CookPilot demonstration recipe (not physically tested). Appliance: air-fryer. Compatible on paper with: AF101, AF300EU. Serves 2. Ingredients: 4 Bone-in, skin-on chicken thighs; 1 tbsp Olive oil; 1 Lemon; 2 clove Garlic cloves, finely grated; 2 tsp Fresh thyme leaves; 1 tsp Fine sea salt; Black pepper 1. Pat the chicken thighs very dry with kitchen paper. Mix the oil, lemon zest, garlic, thyme, salt and pepper, then rub it all over the chicken, including under the skin. 2. Preheat the air fryer on Air Fry at 200 °C for 3 minutes. [air-fry, 200 °C, 3 min] 3. Place the thighs skin-side down in a single layer. Cook for 12 minutes. [air-fry, 200 °C, 12 min] 4.' where exists (select 1 from public.knowledge_documents where id = '00000000-0000-4000-8000-d0c000000012') on conflict (document_id, position) do nothing;
insert into public.knowledge_chunks (document_id, position, content) select '00000000-0000-4000-8000-d0c000000012', 1, '200 °C, 3 min] 3. Place the thighs skin-side down in a single layer. Cook for 12 minutes. [air-fry, 200 °C, 12 min] 4.
Turn the thighs skin-side up and cook for 10–12 minutes more, until the skin is deep golden and the thickest part reaches 74 °C. [air-fry, 200 °C, 11 min] 5. Rest for 5 minutes, squeeze over the lemon juice and serve. [5 min] Safety: Poultry is safe to eat once the thickest part reaches 74 °C (165 °F). Use a thermometer rather than colour. Wash hands, boards and utensils after handling raw chicken.' where exists (select 1 from public.knowledge_documents where id = '00000000-0000-4000-8000-d0c000000012') on conflict (document_id, position) do nothing;

