insert into public.knowledge_chunks (document_id, position, content) select '00000000-0000-4000-8000-d0c000000014', 0, '[recipe:00000000-0000-4000-8000-0ec100000003]
Honey & thyme roasted carrots. Tender, lightly caramelised carrots finished with honey and thyme. Simple enough for a Tuesday, pretty enough for guests.
CookPilot demonstration recipe (not physically tested). Appliance: air-fryer. Compatible on paper with: AF101, AF300EU. Serves 2.
Ingredients: 400 g Carrots; 1 tbsp Olive oil; 2 tsp Honey; 3 sprig Fresh thyme sprigs; 0.5 tsp Fine sea salt
1. Toss the carrots with the olive oil and salt.
2. Cook on Roast at 190 °C for 12 minutes, shaking the basket halfway through. [roast, 190 °C, 12 min]
3. Drizzle over the honey, add the thyme and toss. Cook for 3–4 minutes more, until glossy and tender when pierced with a knife. [roast, 190 °C, 3 min 30 s]
Safety: Honey is not suitable for children under one year old.' where exists (select 1 from public.knowledge_documents where id = '00000000-0000-4000-8000-d0c000000014') on conflict (document_id, position) do nothing;

insert into public.knowledge_documents (id, title, source, source_url, manufacturer, model_number, language, doc_type, published_at, verification_status, rights_note, content_hash)
values ('00000000-0000-4000-8000-d0c000000015', 'Salmon fillets with lemon & dill', 'CookPilot demonstration recipes', null, null, null, 'en', 'recipe', '2026-11-09', 'partial', 'Original CookPilot recipe. Demonstration content, not physically tested.', 'c708898dddee87f6fbd2ee706f656197ef36a96699215a0e7ebb5749c7292390')
on conflict do nothing;
insert into public.knowledge_chunks (document_id, position, content) select '00000000-0000-4000-8000-d0c000000015', 0, '[recipe:00000000-0000-4000-8000-0ec100000004]
Salmon fillets with lemon & dill. Just-cooked salmon with a crisp top and a quick lemon-dill dressing. On the table in a quarter of an hour.
CookPilot demonstration recipe (not physically tested). Appliance: air-fryer. Compatible on paper with: AF101, AF300EU. Serves 2.
Ingredients: 2 Salmon fillets, skin on; 2 tsp Olive oil; 0.5 tsp Fine sea salt; 1 tbsp Lemon juice; 1 tbsp Chopped fresh dill
1. Pat the salmon dry, rub with half the oil and season with salt.
2. Cook skin-side down on Air Fry at 200 °C for 8–10 minutes, depending on thickness, until the flesh flakes easily and the centre reaches 63 °C. [air-fry, 200 °C, 9 min]
3. Stir together the lemon juice, dill and remaining oil. Spoon over the salmon and serve straight away.
Safety: Food-safety agencies recommend cooking fish to an internal temperature of 63 °C (145 °F). Contains fish.' where exists (select 1 from public.knowledge_documents where id = '00000000-0000-4000-8000-d0c000000015') on conflict (document_id, position) do nothing;

