insert into public.knowledge_chunks (document_id, position, content) select '00000000-0000-4000-8000-d0c000000016', 0, '[recipe:00000000-0000-4000-8000-0ec100000005] Grilled ribeye with garlic butter. A thick ribeye seared on a hot grill plate and finished with garlic-parsley butter. Cook to temperature, not to time. CookPilot demonstration recipe (not physically tested). Appliance: indoor-grill. Compatible on paper with: AG301. Serves 2. Ingredients: 500 g Ribeye steak, 3 cm thick; 2 tsp Neutral oil with a high smoke point; 1 tsp Flaky sea salt; 30 g Butter, softened; 1 clove Garlic clove, finely grated; 1 tbsp Chopped flat-leaf parsley 1. Mash the butter with the garlic and parsley and set aside. Pat the steak dry, rub with oil and season generously with salt. 2. Fit the grill plate, close the lid and preheat on Grill, HIGH, until the appliance signals it is ready. [grill, HIGH] 3. Lay the steak on the plate, close the lid and grill for 4 minutes. [grill, HIGH, 4 min] 4.' where exists (select 1 from public.knowledge_documents where id = '00000000-0000-4000-8000-d0c000000016') on conflict (document_id, position) do nothing;
insert into public.knowledge_chunks (document_id, position, content) select '00000000-0000-4000-8000-d0c000000016', 1, 'is ready. [grill, HIGH] 3. Lay the steak on the plate, close the lid and grill for 4 minutes. [grill, HIGH, 4 min] 4.
Flip and grill for 3–5 minutes more. Start checking early: remove at 52–54 °C for medium-rare (it will rise a few degrees while resting), or 63 °C for the officially recommended doneness. [grill, HIGH, 4 min] 5. Top with the garlic butter and rest for 5 minutes before slicing against the grain. [5 min] Safety: Food-safety agencies recommend 63 °C (145 °F) plus a 3-minute rest for whole cuts of beef. Medium-rare is below that; it is a personal choice and not advised for pregnant, elderly or immunocompromised people. Grilling fatty cuts produces smoke — keep the appliance clear of cupboards and ventilate the kitchen. Contains milk (butter).' where exists (select 1 from public.knowledge_documents where id = '00000000-0000-4000-8000-d0c000000016') on conflict (document_id, position) do nothing;

