insert into public.knowledge_chunks (document_id, position, content) select '00000000-0000-4000-8000-d0c000000018', 0, '[recipe:00000000-0000-4000-8000-0ec100000007] Vanilla bean ice cream. A no-cook cream cheese base that turns into a smooth, scoopable vanilla ice cream. Make the base today, spin it tomorrow. CookPilot demonstration recipe (not physically tested). Appliance: frozen-dessert-maker. Compatible on paper with: NC301, NC300EU. Serves 4. Ingredients: 15 g Full-fat cream cheese, softened; 65 g Caster sugar; 1 Vanilla pod, seeds scraped; 180 ml Double (heavy) cream; 240 ml Whole milk 1. Whisk the cream cheese, sugar and vanilla seeds into a smooth paste. Gradually whisk in the cream and milk until the sugar has dissolved. 2. Pour into the pint without going over the max fill line. Close the lid and freeze on a level surface for 24 hours. [24 h] 3. Remove the lid, lock the pint into the outer bowl and the machine, and run the Ice Cream program. [ice-cream] 4.' where exists (select 1 from public.knowledge_documents where id = '00000000-0000-4000-8000-d0c000000018') on conflict (document_id, position) do nothing;
insert into public.knowledge_chunks (document_id, position, content) select '00000000-0000-4000-8000-d0c000000018', 1, 'h] 3. Remove the lid, lock the pint into the outer bowl and the machine, and run the Ice Cream program. [ice-cream] 4.
If the texture is crumbly, add a tablespoon of milk and process once more. Serve straight away. Safety: Contains milk. Never process a pint that was frozen at an angle or filled above the max line.' where exists (select 1 from public.knowledge_documents where id = '00000000-0000-4000-8000-d0c000000018') on conflict (document_id, position) do nothing;

insert into public.knowledge_documents (id, title, source, source_url, manufacturer, model_number, language, doc_type, published_at, verification_status, rights_note, content_hash)
values ('00000000-0000-4000-8000-d0c000000019', 'Mango & lime sorbet', 'CookPilot demonstration recipes', null, null, null, 'en', 'recipe', '2026-11-09', 'partial', 'Original CookPilot recipe. Demonstration content, not physically tested.', '7abcc7db7db91e5f6059fe9f4e8f3180728ce4de4853cd66ed3576f63ea490aa')
on conflict do nothing;
insert into public.knowledge_chunks (document_id, position, content) select '00000000-0000-4000-8000-d0c000000019', 0, '[recipe:00000000-0000-4000-8000-0ec100000008]
Mango & lime sorbet. Three ingredients, intensely fruity and naturally dairy-free. The lime keeps the mango bright.
CookPilot demonstration recipe (not physically tested). Appliance: frozen-dessert-maker. Compatible on paper with: NC301, NC300EU. Serves 4.
Ingredients: 400 g Ripe mango flesh; 40 g Caster sugar; 2 tbsp Lime juice
1. Blend the mango, sugar and lime juice to a completely smooth purée.
2. Pour into the pint up to the max fill line, tap to remove air pockets, close and freeze on a level surface for 24 hours. [24 h]
3. Remove the lid, lock the pint into the machine and run the Sorbet program. [sorbet]
4. If it looks powdery, add a tablespoon of water or juice and process again until smooth.
Safety: Never process a pint that was frozen at an angle or filled above the max line.' where exists (select 1 from public.knowledge_documents where id = '00000000-0000-4000-8000-d0c000000019') on conflict (document_id, position) do nothing;

